WEBVTT

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.090
I've... never seen anything like this.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.710
My glasses...

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.210
I can't see... I can't see...!

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.460
Don't they seem kinda amateurish?

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.010
I'm still a sucker for such
wide-eyed innocence!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.010
Kazu, is this... her?

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.210
Yup.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.760
Let's go, Peaches!

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.960
I want us to do this same
routine at the school festival!

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.460
It was the very first one my
parents performed in college.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.880
So your 'rents were a
cheerleader and her coach...

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.590
How wonderful to have a
memento of their performance.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.510
They must have been an amazing team
if they competed in world championships.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.630
They told me about this all the time.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:13.670
How at the very beginning they only had
seven members, but lived every day to the fullest.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.300
I get it! So that's why you were
so fixated on the number seven.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.170
Of course! This saves us the time
of choreographing a routine ourselves!

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.340
Well, I don't think that's the point.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:32.210
I thought this routine
would be good for our debut.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.460
Let's do it!

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.800
All seven of us!

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.920
Yeah!

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.920
Then it's settled.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.050
We'll have to work hard.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:47.630
We have about two months, so if we
practice like crazy it should all work out.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.800
Besides, we have the
Prince of Tumbling with us!

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.090
The hardest part of this
routine is the first stunt.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.090
The flyer has to do a mid-air backflip.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:04.710
Since we only need one stunt group this time,
I'd like to make sure we nail this backflip.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.630
Kazu, you can do it, right?

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:10.260
I'm not the only candidate for this stunt.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.130
Right, Haru?

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.050
But I...

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.210
We're the Breakers, aren't we?

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.170
Let's break through together!

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.210
There you have it.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:29.550
Then let's choose our flyer after seeing
how you two do over summer break.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.050
Wataru, I'm coming in.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:37.460
Please excuse me for disturbing
you during your video research.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.460
I appreciate all you've done for Wataru.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.920
Dinner is served.
Would you care to join us?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.550
You two look super alike!

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.420
Yeah, and you have a super huge house!

00:02:53.150 --> 00:03:00.030
Mizoguchi    Traditional    Japanese    Cuisine

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.710
Yeah, and you have a super huge house!

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:00.010
And we're super hungry!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:22.460
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.510
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:32.210
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:36.300
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:42.130
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.420
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.630
<i>With that first step</i>

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.840
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.800
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.380
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.010
<i>just as you are</i>

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.170
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:08.670
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.300
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.170
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.420
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:23.550
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.510
Delivery!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.760
Wuh?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.840
--Ichiro, you sure you're holdin' up your end?
--'Course I am!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.760
--I'm telling you, just turn a bit and go!
--What are you doing...?!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.550
All right.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.050
More like all wrong! You need
to warn me about stuff like this!

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.130
Well, this is what Dreams was practicing with.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.800
We can't afford to have
second-rate equipment.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.920
Mizoguchi, how much
did all this set you back?

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.920
No idea. I never check the price
of anything while shopping.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.590
What are you, a celebrity?!

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:07.550
But now that we have all this,
we can start getting serious.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.840
All right!

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:13.210
Let's practice our butts off and win over
the whole women's cheerleading team!

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.590
1, 2, down, up!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.630
I... I'm sorry.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.170
It's not that I don't trust the bases.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:29.340
My mind gets it, but...

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.050
Look, it's fine.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.760
You've got the basic idea
of the Elevator down,

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.260
so I think you and Kazu should
start practicing jumps and flips.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.090
Right!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.260
Okay.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.630
Ready?

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:47.550
Push down without bending
your knees too much,

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.630
then jump while fully extending your legs
and raising your hands right over your head.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:56.260
Once you feel steady, hug your
knees and flip backward.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.130
Kazu looks like he'll be fine.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.260
You're next, Haru. Can you do it?

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.550
Crouch down!

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:22.210
It's all right if you stick to
small jumps until you're used to it.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:23.550
Let's not rush into this.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.840
Okay.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.670
Haru.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.510
Feel like you can you break through?

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.130
Yeah.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.450
Chinese I
Pronunciation Test

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.090
<i>Ta jiang yu ci jieshu</i>!

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:36.950
Chinese I
Pronunciation Test

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:37.000
Chinese I
Pronunciation Test

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.080
Chinese I
Pronunciation Test

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.760
Go, fight, win!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:38.750
Chinese I
Pronunciation Test

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.130
Yes, thank you.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:49.670
It's good to see such enthusiasm,
but that was a disastrous speech, no?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:07:01.550
By the way, next semester my boy will be
studyin' here, so please be nice to him.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.300
Thanks for waiting! Here's your
shaved ice with a sunflower theme!

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.420
Let's eat!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.630
Not even brain freeze
makes you lose your cool!

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.590
Where are Mizoguchi and Ton?

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.460
They have one class left.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.260
Man, thanks to Kazu, I took
a full load last semester.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.550
Just what I'd expect from an
honor student! You over-achiever!

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.960
So, Haru, you takin' the
make-up exam for Chinese?

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.380
It's not a make-up exam!

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.590
Starting tomorrow, we'll practice
in the park during the morning,

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.420
then after lunch, we'll move to the roof.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.840
We're gonna eat, sleep, and breathe
cheerleading this summer.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.460
Ichiro.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:51.210
I haven't seen you wear
that wristband before.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.710
Yeah, ain't it neat?

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.170
What's goin' on here, Romeo?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.550
I got it from my cute girlfriend!

00:07:58.550 --> 00:07:59.050
Not.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:00.710
Like I even have one!

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.420
Show me your wrist!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.510
Ow!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:13.420
Oh, this. I just sprained it at work.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.170
Why didn't you tell us earlier?!

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:17.630
How long will it take to heal up?

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:22.170
The doctor said it'll take about four weeks,
but for sumthin' like this, I can make it two.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:26.130
Then that means stunts and tumbling
are off-limits for four weeks.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:30.210
Don't be stupid! If I just tape it up
properly, I'll be perfectly fine!

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.340
No.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:34.510
We're about to start tossing
and catching practice.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.170
You can't risk aggravating it
or getting another injury.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:41.170
Hmph. Well, fine then.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.460
1, 2, down, up, down, up!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.550
Gen, your grip is loose.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.420
Use the force from the load-in
to propel him all the way up.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.510
Ton, you're still not using
your knees well enough.

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.170
--Right!
--Okay!

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.760
Mizoguchi, during the cradle,
watch the flyer more carefully,

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.380
and catch him with your
whole body, not just your arms.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.630
Understood!

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:14.800
Kazu, your prep jump is too big.
And you can't control your posture mid-air.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.010
Pay more attention to your body's axis.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.550
Got it!

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.340
Right, one more time!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.670
Morning.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.760
Morning!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.670
So you managed to wake up early.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:47.170
Thanks for inviting me
to practice with you.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:51.880
The two of us practiced together
a lot back when we did judo.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.460
That's right.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:57.010
I guess it's just better to practice
together than by yourself.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.420
And as fellow flyers, it's worth the effort.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.670
Kazu, I--

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.510
You can fly, Haru.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.590
I've been watching you for a long time.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:15.590
You made judo techniques you
struggled with into your specialty, right?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.840
I did them with you,
so I know I'm not wrong.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.090
Kazu! I will fly!

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:27.170
Yeah! And I don't plan on handing
over the flyer's part, either!

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:29.590
Bandou Gym

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:36.510
It's fine if you just do
a straight jump first.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.840
1, 2, down, up!

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:43.460
Haru!

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.010
I... I'm sorry!

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:53.880
I guess I'll go review it
some more on the trampoline.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:14.920
One more time!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.260
Go! Let's go, Breakers!

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:24.630
We are B-O-Y!

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.960
Go! Let's go, Breakers!

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.340
1, 2, 3! Are you ready?

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.710
--Go!
--Stop!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.760
The dancing, the motions...

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.710
No matter how long we stand here,
we just can't get in sync.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:44.760
I'm sorry, it's because I can't keep up.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:48.170
I'd no idea my sense of
rhythm was this bad...

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.210
It's all right.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:53.050
If you pay close attention to the counting,
harmonize your movements,

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:54.630
and watch how your teammates--

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.760
That's all wicked hard!

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:03.630
I wonder if our debut will go well.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.840
Let's call it a day.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.260
Why?!

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:12.300
If we don't practice more,
we'll never be ready!

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:15.210
Sure, but ain't it smarter to switch
to sumthin' else for a bit?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.010
Isn't now the time to dig in our heels?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.210
But even if we keep pushing
ourselves like this...

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.760
It's just when you think you can't go on
that you show some guts and keep tryin'!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.590
Don't think you can solve every
problem with guts alone.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:29.130
It won't heal your sprain any faster, no?

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:33.420
You call this a sprain?

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.010
Ichiro!

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.300
Damn it!

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.670
Hey, stop!

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.340
Enough already! You're hurtin' yourself!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.710
Get your hands off me. I'm fine now!

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:51.260
Like hell you are! You didn't
sprain that at work, did you?

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:57.380
You got hurt practicin' by yourself.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:01.630
This sucks.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.590
Seriously, why'd I have to get injured?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.170
Why am I the one draggin' the team down?

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:07.670
This is just so stupid!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.260
What are you sayin'?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:13.010
That injury proves just
how hard you practice!

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:16.380
How can you call that stupid?! I mean, I...!

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:23.460
I mean, no amount of guts will
ever let me catch up to you.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.710
The stupidest one here is me!

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:29.760
Then I must be the most pathetic of us all.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:35.590
My body's so big and yet I'm so weak,
and I take the longest to learn anything...

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:40.630
And me... I have no sense of rhythm,
and my movements are so stiff.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:43.840
I'm the one least suited for cheerleading.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.300
H-Hey now...!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.960
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:52.710
When you get right down to it, I'm the one
who suggested we perform this routine...

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.550
You idiots!

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:58.260
Haru?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:13:59.670
Give me a break, Kazu!

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.710
You're the person who got brought everyone
together and charged full speed ahead!

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.130
Ichiro, Gen, don't give me that crap

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.760
when you're both way better athletes
than me! It pisses me off!

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:11.960
And Ton, just who is the
fried pork curry champ here?!

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:12.960
--Four-Eyes!
--Four--!

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:16.760
Your brainy quotes always fall flat, but once
in a while you have something good to say!

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:21.010
Sho, aside from your Risujiro obsession and complete
lack of fashion sense, I've got no complaints!

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:23.840
You're all already cool enough!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.380
I'm the one who's having to try the hardest!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:33.800
I have no choice but to
believe that I can do it!

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:34.800
I can!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.550
I can do it!

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.420
We all can do it!

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:40.170
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:41.880
Go, fight, win!

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.710
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.760
Go, fight, win!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.550
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:49.590
Go, fight, win!

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.460
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.130
Go, fight, win!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.130
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.840
Go, fight, win!

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.920
Let's go, Breakers!

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.590
Go, fight, win!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.510
Let's go, Breakers!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:04.090
Go, fight, win!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.010
--G-Guys...
--Let's go, Breakers!

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.880
--G-Guys...
--Go, fight, win!

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.760
Let's go, Breakers!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.460
Go, fight, win!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:13.510
Let's go, Breakers!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.340
Go, fight, win!

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.260
Let's go, Breakers!

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.010
Go, fight, win!

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:23.630
Let's gooo, Breakers!

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:30.840
I don't really get what just
happened, but I feel great!

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.920
Ditto!

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:33.670
Kazu!

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.050
Yeah?

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.670
I feel like I could fly now.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:42.300
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.340
1, 2, down, up, down, up!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.090
Catch him!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.590
Are you all right?

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.630
Haru?

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.300
That felt different.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:01.420
You're supporting me, all of you.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.590
I'll trust you and fly.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.170
Let me try again!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.630
--Sure!
--Yeah!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.130
Here I go!

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:18.460
1, 2, down, up, down, up!

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:29.510
Haru!

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.800
You did it!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.840
You flew!

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:32.760
That was fantastic!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.630
You've opened a new door!

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.840
Opened it up wide!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.130
Not half bad! Right?

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:44.840
Yes, it was a beautiful backflip.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:47.210
I did it...

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.920
I did it.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:51.380
I did it!

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:12.090
Hi there! The Breakers will
take the stage at 1PM sharp!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.960
This ain't no joke! It's Men's Cheerleading!

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:16.760
--Come and watch us!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.800
--What are you doing? Huh? Men's Cheerleading?!
--Come and watch us!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.460
I'll definitely come see you!

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.510
We're the Men's Cheerleading Club!

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:24.880
We're performing at 1PM!

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:27.300
'Round and 'round and 'round and...

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.840
Does your stomach hurt?
Did you eat too much?

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.210
That's not my problem...

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:34.050
We're the Men's Cheerleading Club!
Please come watch us!

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.170
We're the Men's Cheerleading Club!
We're performing today!

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.010
We start at 1PM!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.880
Please come watch!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.630
Please come watch!

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.010
It's been a while!

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.670
Chihiro... Sakai?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.760
Let's see... Haru, was it?

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.010
Uh, yes!

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.460
Blond hair suits you!

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.210
Oh, does it--

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:58.090
Yes, yes!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.420
This is my boy, Haru!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.010
Kazu, what the hell!

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.460
Don't jump me like that!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:07.420
Oh no, did I make you mad?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.840
Both of our performances
start at the same time.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.760
I wanted to watch Breakers' debut.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.960
And Haru wanted to go watch Dreams!

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.380
It's really too bad.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:21.050
Well, let's both do our best!

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.670
Yeah...

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.050
What?!

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.510
She's cute, isn't she?

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.260
Good luck, Haru, my boy!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.090
It's time to go! I'm not waiting for you!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.050
--Hey, Haru, hold up--
--Whoa!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.550
Ow...

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.760
I'm sorry!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.590
You okay?

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:51.760
Thank y--

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.260
Sorry about that!

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.420
Breakers...

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:01.670
Big bro!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.200
Caf

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.200
Sunflower

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:09.630
Welcome! We're taking last
orders for the day, so...

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.090
Oh!

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.340
<b>Men's
Cheerleading
Team
Breakers
First
Performance!!</b>

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:13.790
<b>Men's
Cheerleading
Team
Breakers
First
Performance!!</b>

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.250
<b>Men's
Cheerleading
Team
Breakers
First
Performance!!</b>

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:14.460
<b>Men's
Cheerleading
Team
Breakers
First
Performance!!</b>

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.210
Ah, this is bad!
I'm gettin' super nervous!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.510
Idiot! Don't say that,
you'll make me nervous!

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:25.920
That's the point!

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:26.960
Why?!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.380
These contacts keep rolling
'round and 'round and 'round and...

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.840
If only you'd practiced
with them beforehand.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:36.210
Well, it's impossible not to feel
nervous before our first performance.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:37.880
I'm a wreck, too.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:38.880
Same.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:42.130
But we've come this far, so we
just have to give it our all!

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:42.880
Yeah!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:43.800
That's right!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:47.630
I just gotta go out there and make
all the girls scream their heads off!

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:49.170
That goes for me, too!

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:51.920
I would also like to make them go wild.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.050
Ton, what have you been up to?

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.760
Oh, sorry!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:02.710
I just got a message saying my
girlfriend can't come see us today.

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:11.090
Breakers, you're on standby!

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.670
Okay! Let's huddle up!

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.840
Don't look so down.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.050
To think that you're our dark horse.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.590
I'm about to lose my faith in humanity.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:23.840
I guess this is the end of Cherry Boys.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.090
Don't worry!

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:30.050
If you show how cool you are onstage,
you're sure to pick up a girl or two!

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:32.380
What? Two girlfriends?

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:34.050
Maybe.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:39.010
Let's break it all to smithereens, guys.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:45.340
Go, fight, win!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:49.050
Let's gooo, Breakers!

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.010
Hello, everyone!

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:03.300
We're the Men's Cheerleading
Team, Breakers!

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:09.510
Today we're making our debut.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:13.260
We'll do our best to make you smile,

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:15.260
so please enjoy the performers!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.460
Uh, please enjoy the performance!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:28.630
Begin!

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:42.170
I've never seen so far.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:47.760
Let's go! Go!

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.130
Meishiin! Hey! C'mon!

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:51.630
We are the Breakers!

00:21:51.630 --> 00:21:53.300
This is showtime!

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.920
We feel great!

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:58.090
B-R-E-A-K-E-R-S!

00:21:58.090 --> 00:22:01.710
Gooo Breakers!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.210
--Welcome! We are B-O-Y!
--The soft spring of muscle passing from our palms,

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:10.960
--Welcome! We are B-O-Y!
--the exchange of glances,

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:14.210
--C'mon! Let's go, Breakers!
--the exchange of glances,

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:15.590
--We are...!
--the exchange of glances,

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:18.920
--We are...!
--the sound of our breath...

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:22.130
Go! Let's go, Breakers!

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:25.260
1, 2, 3! Are you ready?

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:26.920
C'mon, fans!

00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:28.130
Follow us!

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:30.840
Say black and yellow!

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:33.960
You say black and yellow!

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:34.800
Okay!

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:39.050
3, 2, 3, 2, 1, go!

00:23:00.340 --> 00:23:01.760
Yeah!

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:07.920
It's still not perfect...

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:12.340
But right now, we're giving it our all!

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:20.380
Go, Breakers!

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:34.300
The Breakers were great, weren't they!

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:37.050
Men's Cheerleading is so cool!

00:23:42.340 --> 00:23:45.550
All-men's Cheerleading?

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:48.940
<b>Men's
Cheerleading
Team
Breakers
First
Performance!!</b>

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:48.920
Breakers...

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:58.130
"Dream as if you'll live forever.
Live as if you'll die today."

00:23:58.130 --> 00:24:00.170
Those are the perfect words
to describe us right now.

00:24:00.170 --> 00:24:02.760
We need to practice as if
everything begins and ends today.

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:06.630
And since we have more members,
we'll have to push ourselves hard.

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.970
Next Episode: Restart.

00:24:09.090 --> 00:24:10.960
Let's go, Breakers!
